  "finding": "For the 10 in-tree Daniel-CPVC pigments (CPVC 0.4183-0.6365) the reduced-PVC arithmetic is exact and zero-parameter: below CPVC porosity is identically 0 (consistent with the barrier module's void-free Fickian assumption), and above CPVC porosity onsets FIRST-ORDER in relative PVC overshoot (pi = eps/(1+eps): a +5% PVC error at CPVC already creates 4.76 vol% air voids), so CPVC is a cliff, not a soft optimum. Above CPVC the module's void-free coverage/DFT arithmetic mis-reads film build by exactly LAMBDA and dry-film density by exactly 1/LAMBDA: an iron-oxide-red epoxy-polyamide primer formulated at PVC 0.50 (CPVC 0.4183, LAMBDA 1.195) delivers +19.5% DFT and -16.3% dry-film density versus the void-free arithmetic. Porosity uncertainty inherited from a declared +/-10% oil-absorption band is u(pi) ~= 0.02-0.05 at LAMBDA 1.2 (GUM LPU validated by 400k-draw MC on all 10 pigments), comparable to the porosity created by a 5% PVC overshoot -- so near CPVC, OA data quality and PVC metering discipline are co-equal load-bearing controls.",
